{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"RECORD-PLACEMENT INDEX + operator anti-pattern ruling (2026-08-12). No comment deleted — the store is append-only and the originals stay exactly where they are; this comment redirects future readers to the durable home of each record.\n\nOPERATOR RULING. This ticket accumulated cross-cutting ops and analysis records that had nothing to do with its own deliverable. Verbatim: \"why are we storing this information in a scratchpad ticket rather than in a rebar session log or in the tickets we are using to actually complete the work? this smells like an anti-pattern.\" It is an anti-pattern, and future sessions must not repeat it. The rule going forward: a session-scoped investigation belongs in a `rebar session-log`; a record that informs a specific piece of work belongs as a comment on the ticket doing that work; a work ticket's comments are for ITS deliverable only.\n\nWHERE EACH RECORD NOW LIVES. Session log for this bug-bash session's ops/analysis records: cosey-vinegarish-mouflon (d0d8-9dfe-f2d8-4364).\n\n- Comment 10 (2026-08-12T10:55:29Z) — \"Why the code-review severity axes are inert\", zero-LLM root cause over 1,545 code_review sidecars. Class: session-scoped analysis. -> session log entry 1 (full copy). Pointer also posted on fixable-angular-caribou, the ordinal->kind-set migration story, because the pending P3.0 blocking-lane decision (which criteria should be blocking-enabled, and the threshold/aggregation fix) references this analysis; it has no better single owning ticket than the session log.\n- Comment 11 (2026-08-12T20:11:47Z) — deprecation removal-readiness survey. Class: session-scoped analysis with per-item work owners. -> session log entry 2 (summary, with the Tier 1-4 findings preserved). Per-item cross-reference comments posted on the tickets that acted on it: checked-unhelpful-tanager (Tier 1 gitattributes arm), priceless-charred-fruitbat (single-pass review surfaces, incl. the finding that _review_ticket_impl must STAY), slowmotion-stricken-mare (REBAR_LLM_MODEL supersession), and salted-growable-murrelet (the LIVE reconciler.resolved_statuses vs inert jira.resolved_statuses distinction, for its pending operator sign-off).\n- Comment 12 (2026-08-12T22:48:29Z) — AWS alarm sweep 04:00Z->22:45Z. Class: ops investigation. -> session log entry 3 (full copy) + substantive cross-reference on greasy-plucky-piranha (the alarm family's diagnostic home), with the acting tickets cross-referenced: unskillful-supportive-lion (the deferred_for 1810/1820/1810/1930s vs bound=1800s data supporting the bound raise) and unheedful-unfair-sloth (the JIRA_API_TOKEN expiry producing zero alarms — the bridge coverage gap).\n- Comment 13 (2026-08-12T23:22:57Z) — alarm sweep addendum, the 23:07Z false-positive firing pair. Class: ops investigation. -> session log entry 4 (full copy) + covered in the greasy-plucky-piranha cross-reference. Bugs already filed at the time: widespread-zealous-narwhal (e2a6-9ee4-8d5c-4290) and colossal-slothful-grouse (8c2f-8377-5044-4650), both in infra/scripts/observability.sh.\n\nWHAT CORRECTLY STAYS HERE (this ticket's own deliverable): comments 1-6, the cost-analysis experiment rounds 1-6; comment 7, the CloudWatch quantification of the Bedrock error blast radius — ops-flavored but explicitly attributable to the model-comparison experiments run UNDER this ticket and carried forward into the lever option book (the cheap-model-fails-silently alarm observation and the DeepSeek ceiling flag); and comments 8-9, the closeout and the recorded close-deferral disposition.\n\nSTATUS UNCHANGED. This ticket remains OPEN per comment 9's disposition, and its description was not edited (attestation currency)."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786588815138840001,"uuid":"9d17fcec-352c-4a04-9520-ff960b9b50ba"}